f853" "q-77547/selection/2194a749e03681ff65b6ea6ea32970b75b53bb97108ed694957c7fb88e1f6061" "q-77547/selection/473fc46ee1cba3e1896ff9a59d348388466b49bf8249cbeb4b07f764515814ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77547" :question/id #uuid "711300c3-0b93-5c10-812e-3a69e9246478" :question/math-academy-id "q-77547" :question/problem "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ \\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77547/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77548/selection/5adfd53be4e81a50d